                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e9207b2-fb3a-3441-9873-e7917e707707",
                        "entry_id": "a8680bfb-825f-3eab-984b-7798ea32a053",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. жрец, прорицатель у древних римлян, толковавший волю богов на основании ауспиций, то есть по поведению птиц; птицегадатель"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "756b8af7-d3db-4a3a-9fb2-3c42c0a20b32",
                                "sense_id": "2e9207b2-fb3a-3441-9873-e7917e707707",
                                "text": "Авгуры последних времен Римской империи не могли без смеха взирать друг на друга и между тем все-таки продолжали ремесло свое."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d8b0cae3-83f7-3060-9047-ec3cbf13dc9a",
                        "entry_id": "a8680bfb-825f-3eab-984b-7798ea32a053",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ирон. человек, который кичится своими «особыми» знаниями, превращает их в тайну для других людей, выражает свои мысли языком, непонятным для «непосвящённых»"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d9f9cbd-17e3-4eee-8bf9-3508f90b72b6",
                                "sense_id": "d8b0cae3-83f7-3060-9047-ec3cbf13dc9a",
                                "text": "Ваше преосвященство! Давайте побеседуем. Когда сенатор и епископ смотрят друг на друга, они не могут не перемигнуться. Мы с вами — два авгура. Сейчас я сделаю вам одно признание: у меня есть своя философия."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "93df4d6b-fb97-4b6c-84f3-810f553c4eca",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8680bfb-825f-3eab-984b-7798ea32a053",
                        "target_lang_word": "augur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "augur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09e377c6-02b4-3be7-831e-e5032501137a",
                                        "entry_id": "66418481-fa89-3382-b1cc-f6096c4bce0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A diviner who foretells events by the behaviour of birds or other animals, or by signs derived from celestial phenomena, or unusual occurrences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28c823f3-8ede-43cd-bd41-b0c6527b10a0",
                                                "sense_id": "09e377c6-02b4-3be7-831e-e5032501137a",
                                                "text": "Augur of ill, whoſe tongue was never found / Without a prieſtly curſe, or boding ſound; [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c48eb3b2-2165-3d63-aef0-5c8e1918bd0f",
                                        "entry_id": "66418481-fa89-3382-b1cc-f6096c4bce0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An official who interpreted omens before the start of public events."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient-Rome"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19de280b-eb05-47f4-8004-e46d41df85dd",
                                                "sense_id": "c48eb3b2-2165-3d63-aef0-5c8e1918bd0f",
                                                "text": "It was an ancient tradition, that when the Capitol was founded by one of the Roman kings, the god Terminus (who presided over boundaries, and was represented, according to the fashion of that age, by a large stone) alone, among all the inferior deities, refused to yield his place to Jupiter himself. A favorable inference was drawn from his obstinacy, which was interpreted by the augurs as a sure presage that the boundaries of the Roman power would never recede."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "augur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8f3a80e-ba5a-392f-ac6d-a9cc2eece564",
                                        "entry_id": "573fe7fa-b32b-322e-a41e-a101f533f4aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To foretell events; to exhibit signs of future events; to indicate a favorable or an unfavorable outcome."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27db294d-f7ce-4446-b55e-8902649df3c2",
                                                "sense_id": "d8f3a80e-ba5a-392f-ac6d-a9cc2eece564",
                                                "text": "to augur well or ill"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbee7b27-e916-4fc9-997b-47b8deacb61b",
                                                "sense_id": "d8f3a80e-ba5a-392f-ac6d-a9cc2eece564",
                                                "text": "But there, too, the meteorological omens augured ill."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de566357-5cdc-4944-8fcf-2e373c681506",
                                                "sense_id": "d8f3a80e-ba5a-392f-ac6d-a9cc2eece564",
                                                "text": "Whether term limits would augur a return of justices with broader experience in public life is debatable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "042eb14c-1f39-40a9-8882-2b5d6c678f89",
                                                "sense_id": "d8f3a80e-ba5a-392f-ac6d-a9cc2eece564",
                                                "text": "As Ellmann was quietly assembling materials for his biography, specialization was on the rise in American literature departments, as the critic Erich Auerbach warned, auguring the decline of a general humanities education."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9ad278a9-8fe7-4d3d-bfea-04407d69e2ca",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8680bfb-825f-3eab-984b-7798ea32a053",
                        "target_lang_word": "soothsayer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "soothsayer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e83f1c1d-fc52-3a3e-848d-ed3a3a0907ca",
                                        "entry_id": "7a972419-d297-396d-9f98-c75ebb7ddaff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who attempts to predict the future, using magic, intuition or intelligence; a diviner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc0f4fb5-5981-4eee-bb1c-3f8b20532623",
                                                "sense_id": "e83f1c1d-fc52-3a3e-848d-ed3a3a0907ca",
                                                "text": "It is a great pleasure to be with you today and to speak to you concerning the future of medicine. In so doing, I do not wish to pose as a soothsayer or crystal gazer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb74f6f7-4464-4302-9288-05ef21fa330f",
                                                "sense_id": "e83f1c1d-fc52-3a3e-848d-ed3a3a0907ca",
                                                "text": "The past twenty years have seen their share of soothsayers ready to predict with conviction one extreme or another of the alternative futures I have presented."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67188317-4338-306b-bec3-173314633a8f",
                                        "entry_id": "7a972419-d297-396d-9f98-c75ebb7ddaff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mantis (Mantodea spp.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8ac0a9c-b098-3db3-9fd1-2a8be669ee38",
                                        "entry_id": "7a972419-d297-396d-9f98-c75ebb7ddaff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who tells the truth; a truthful person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46c1f99a-2b68-32bf-bf50-508913b7f88c",
                                        "entry_id": "7a972419-d297-396d-9f98-c75ebb7ddaff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A double dart moth (Graphiphora augur)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2bfa35b0-6c57-4393-8fc9-3e450c082b9b",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8680bfb-825f-3eab-984b-7798ea32a053",
